The `ap_int.h` header isn't available in the compilation environment. Since wide bus types aren't supported, I should revert to using plain `double*` pointers but keep all the other optimizations (tiling, double-buffering, pipeline, unroll, array partitioning) and add the burst length pragmas on the m_axi interfaces to get the memory coalescing benefit without requiring unavailable headers.

